        "PAPSS is the oldest of the three. Designed by Afreximbank together with the AfCFTA Secretariat, it was commercially launched in Accra on 13 January 2022. The idea is simple: a Lagos bank paying a Nairobi supplier on behalf of an importer settles in naira, the supplier receives shillings, and clearing takes place between African banks, with Afreximbank acting as settlement agent and providing guarantees and overdraft facilities to participants. At launch, according to [Engineering News](https://www.engineeringnews.co.za/article/pan-african-payment-and-settlement-system-to-save-5bn-a-year-in-transaction-costs-2022-01-14), more than 80% of cross-border payments originating from African banks had to be routed through correspondent banks outside the continent and cleared in dollars or euros, and the system's promoters estimated that PAPSS could save more than $5 billion a year in transaction costs.",
