        "Rising perceived risks reinforce that retreat. 48% of executives list geopolitics among their main concerns, six points more than a year earlier, and the share reaches 63% in groups operating in several countries, against 41% in 2025; liquidity risk is cited by 29% of respondents, eleven points more. For a banking group present in Côte d'Ivoire, Mali and Nigeria at once, the exit of the three AES countries from ECOWAS, tensions between Abuja and Ouagadougou and road blockades imposed by armed groups in the Sahel weigh on the value of its subsidiaries. The new infrastructure lowers the cost of transactions between countries; it does not lower the political uncertainty surrounding those countries.",
