    "excerpt": "Ghanaian farmers are being paid roughly 75% more than their Ivorian neighbours for the 2026-2027 season. The gap is not the product of a policy choice but of two pricing rules with different exposure to timing, and it puts the coordination promised by Abidjan and Accra to the test.",
