    "excerpt": "The closure of the Strait of Hormuz has pushed Brent above $100 and urea nearly 40% higher. In West Africa, the shock does more than separate crude exporters from importers: it divides the countries able to refine and cushion the blow from those forced to choose between their budgets and household purchasing power.",
