    "title": "AfCFTA: a near-universal agreement, a market still to be built",
    "excerpt": "Five years after trading began, 49 states have ratified the African Continental Free Trade Area, yet intra-African trade remains close to 15% of the continent's total. The bottleneck has shifted from tariffs to rules of origin, transaction costs and domestic implementation.",
