          "The comparison with other continents is familiar. According to UNCTAD data compiled by the [Bundeszentrale für politische Bildung](https://www.bpb.de/kurz-knapp/zahlen-und-fakten/globalisierung/247690/intra-und-interregionaler-handel/), 68.9% of European exports stayed in Europe in 2022, 56.1% of Asian exports in Asia and 30.6% of North American exports in North America, against 13.7% for Africa. The usual inference is that Africa trades “too little” with itself and that the agreement will correct the anomaly. The reasoning is too hasty. Europe and East Asia trade among themselves because their economies are large, close, diversified and embedded in production chains that carry the same product across several borders; tariff preferences came afterwards, and they explain only a small part of that trade.",
